  "local_nvme": {
    "claim_class": "measured on a purpose-built A/B cluster pair, not on the workshop cluster",
    "method": "One snapshot of the workshop cluster restored to two clusters, db.r8g.2xlarge and db.r8gd.2xlarge. Verified identical before measuring: 500,000 rows, 1,680 ground truth rows, and all three HNSW indexes at 3905/1302/207 MB. Only the instance class differs.",
    "caveat": "shared_buffers was pinned to 2 GiB on BOTH clusters via a shared cluster parameter group. At the stock 41.5 GiB the 10.6 GiB working set never evicts, idx_blks_read is 0 and the buffer hit rate is 100.000%, so there is no read I/O for a tiered cache to improve. 2 GiB makes the working set 5.3x oversubscribed, which is the regime the feature addresses. This is a stated deviation, not a stock measurement.",
